WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.669
In the quantum
universe, there's

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:06.740
an undiscovered frontier
where the laws of our world

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:11.277
give way to the ones that apply
on the tiniest scale we know.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.647
They're divorced from
our everyday experience.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.083
How can you think
about a world that

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.719
has different rules than ours?

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.388
It's not easy.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.556
That's why I want to
take you to this place

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:26.826
where it's not only possible
to make such a leap.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.862
It's mandatory.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:33.767
It's a world very much like
our own except in one respect.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.637
[ominous music]

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:49.582
It just happens to be
missing a spatial dimension--

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.383
the third one.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.755
In order to venture
into the quantum cosmos,

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:59.092
we have to be able to
imagine another dimension.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.361
That's very hard to do.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:04.097
It's much easier to wrap
your mind around a world

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.865
that's missing one of
the three dimensions

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.567
that we take for granted.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:11.738
The beings of the world we're
about to enter have only two.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:16.576
This world was first imagined
by a man named Edwin Abbott.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:21.448
Everyone and everything here
and everyone they know and love

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.982
is flat.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.218
Their houses are flat.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.053
Some are squares.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.122
Others are triangles.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.957
Some have more complex shapes--

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.026
say, octagons.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.262
But all are completely flat.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.666
They scurry about on foot
or in little vehicles,

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.935
in and out of their
flat buildings,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.237
busy with their flat lives.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:48.041
Everyone on this world
has width and length

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.977
but no height whatsoever.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:55.482
These flatworlders know about
left/right and forward/back.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:02:00.186
But have no hint, not an
inkling, about up/down,

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.288
except for one tiny group--

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:07.760
the mathematicians who
imagined something more.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:12.465
The mathematicians dream of
a world in three dimensions,

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.968
but it's too hard for
most of the flatworlders

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.436
to think about.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:21.241
The mathematician says,
listen, it's really very easy.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.942
We all know left/right.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.878
We all know forward/back.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:28.014
So let's just imagine another
dimension at right angles

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.582
to the other two.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:33.152
But the flatworlders say,
what are you talking about?

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.255
At right angles
to the other two?

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:38.825
Everybody knows that there
can only be two dimensions.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.159
Go ahead, wise guy.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.161
Show us that third dimension.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.031
Where is it?

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.333
So the mathematician
draws a picture.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.209
Poor teacher.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.144
Nobody listens to
mathematicians.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:01.781
[electronic music]

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:06.586
Every creature on
flatworld sees its Fellows

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:09.956
as merely short lines,
which are the nearest

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.692
sides of their oblong bodies.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:15.528
But the insides of a
flatworlder are forever

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:19.766
mysterious unless exposed
by some terrible accident

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.368
or autopsy.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:25.471
And then one day, we came along.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.778
Hello?

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.947
How are you?

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.181
Hi.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:38.685
I'm a visitor from
the third dimension.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.253
Hello?

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.889
I feel sorry for the little guy.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.124
To him, it appears
that my greeting

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:48.161
is emanating from
his own flat body,

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.663
an alien voice from within.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.899
That's because nothing
can come from above.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.602
There is no above in this world.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.770
A three-dimensional
creature like me

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:01.207
can only exist on
flatworld where my feet

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.109
touch the surface of the plane.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.581
Sorry, little guy.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:12.552
I know how weird
this must be for you.

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:13.820
Don't worry.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:18.224
You're on a perfectly safe
trip to a third dimension.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.259
Nothing's going to harm you.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.730
But this is your chance to
see a whole new perspective

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.265
on where you live.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.234
At first, our
flatworlder can make

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.802
no sense of what is happening.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:33.439
It's utterly outside the
realm of flatworld experience.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.475
But eventually, he
realizes that he's

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:39.612
viewing flatworld from a
totally new vantage point--

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:40.880
above.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.583
Now, he can see
into closed rooms.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.219
He can see into
his flat fellows.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.721
This unprecedented
three-dimensional view

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:52.725
of his two-dimensional
universe is devastating.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:55.361
Traveling to another dimension
provides as an incidental

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:58.498
benefit a kind of X-ray vision.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.534
Just as the flat world
houses can have no roofs,

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.903
their inhabitants
can have no sky,

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:08.908
because that sky could only
exist in a third dimension.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.977
Little guy has suffered enough.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:12.211
I'm going to put him down.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.949
From the point of
view of its spouse,

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.551
this flatworlder
has distressingly

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:22.055
disappeared then
unaccountably materialized

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.089
from out of nowhere.

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:27.226
[ominous music]

